# ─── Secrets. Nothing here has ever existed in this repo and nothing should. ──
# Listed anyway because the release process handles a PyPI token, and the cheapest
# moment to block a credential is before it is written, not after it is pushed.
# GitHub secret-scanning push protection is on, but it only knows provider-shaped
# tokens; a file called .env full of anything is invisible to it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.pypirc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
secrets.json

# ─── Local databases — the class of file that already leaked once. ───────────
# `.code-review-graph/graph.db` (848 KB, 4,226 absolute home paths) reached the
# sdist on 2026-08-30 because hatchling does not read NESTED .gitignore files and
# that directory's only protection was its own. Git did respect it, so the file
# was never tracked -- but relying on a tool to write its own ignore rule is
# relying on someone else's implementation detail. The rule is by CLASS, not by
# name, because the next local tool will pick a different directory.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ─── Tool caches whose only protection today is a nested .gitignore ──────────
.code-review-graph/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
